From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:21:47 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] segacd-bios

Before a Sega CD disc starts slot checks the BIOS of the disc's region:
BIOS/bios_CD_U.bin, bios_CD_E.bin or bios_CD_J.bin, 131072 bytes, with a
crc32 slot knows. US: 9f6f6276 (md5 854b9150240a198070150e4566ae1290,
the dump the Genesis Plus GX doc lists) or c6d10268 (md5
2efd74e3232ff260e371b99f84024f7f, the row in libretro-database
dat/System.dat); Europe 529ac15a and Japan 9d2da8f2 (both System.dat).
The region comes from the file name tags, then the byte at 0x20b of a
.cue or .iso data track (0x64 Europe, 0xa1 Japan, anything else USA,
the core's own get_region), then USA, because reading a .chd needs a
hunk decode. A missing file or the wrong size keeps the disc on the
shelf with "Sega CD needs BIOS/bios_CD_U.bin" (E, J), because the core
refuses the disc without it. Another 128 KB file launches with one
"bios_CD_U.bin is not a known dump" toast a session: the core checks
nothing in the file, so a junk BIOS would otherwise be a black screen
with no word. A disc resumed at boot is checked the same way. The six
toasts upload after the FDS ones.
